.TH DISTROCLONE-USB 1 "October 2026" "distroClone USB 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
distroclone-usb \- create a persistent live USB from a live ISO
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B distroclone-usb
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch the GTK desktop to select a live ISO, a USB disk and persistence space.
The selected USB is erased after an explicit confirmation and administrative
authentication. Internal, mounted, read-only and in-use disks are rejected.
The original ISO is stored intact on ext4; a separate ext4 volume stores changes.
.SH SHARED FILES AND ENCRYPTION
New USBs expose Shared in the live user's home and at /Shared.
Choose unencrypted creation, encrypted persistence and Shared, or full encryption
including the ISO. Encryption currently requires a compatible Debian Live or
SysLinuxOS initramfs. Full mode leaves minimal boot code readable, uses a US boot
keyboard and asks separately in GRUB and Linux. Existing USBs are not upgraded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--inspect " ISO
Inspect a live ISO and print JSON without writing media.
.TP
.B --list-devices
Print eligible USB/removable devices and their identities as JSON.
.TP
.BI "--plan " ISO
Validate a read-only creation plan. Requires --device.
.TP
.BI "--device " DEVICE
Whole USB disk used for planning, for example /dev/sdb.
.TP
.BI "--persistence-mib " SIZE
Persistence size in MiB for planning; default 4096, minimum 512.
.TP
.B --check-dependencies
Check required executables and GRUB platform modules.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Supports recognized x86-64 Debian live-boot and Ubuntu/Linux Mint casper desktop
images. MX/antiX is recognized but not supported.
Generated UEFI loaders are unsigned: disable Secure Boot.
